.TH APROCS 1.SH NAMEaprocs \- another process lister.SH SYNOPSIS\fBaprocs\fR[\-anqvV] [\-c=n] [\-m[=sec]] [\-h].SH DESCRIPTION\fBaprocs\fRlists the processes in the system as a tree, each child indented underits parent, with its id, parent, priority, CPU time, age and share ofthe processor.  Version 1.10, by EKF Elektronik, 1996..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-a\fRonly processes using more than 0.1 per cent of the processor..TP 12\fB\-m\fI[=sec]\fRmeasure activity between two moments, three seconds apart unless told..TP 12\fB\-n\fRa plain list, not a tree..TP 12\fB\-c=\fIn\fRcolumns of indent from parent to child; 2 unless told..TP 12\fB\-q\fRfill empty fields with zeros, so the output sorts with\fBqsort9\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-v, \-vv\fRmore detail, or much more..TP 12\fB\-h\fRwhat each column of the output means..TP 12\fB\-V\fRabout aprocs itself..SH SEE ALSOprocs, top